  "interpretation_notes": [
    "Heldout sets are computed for the selected dev/test query sources only (GRAPH_PROTOCOL §2.6 query selection with caps/floors); the mask scope is the global union H_dev ∪ H_test ∪ reverse per §4.1, not per-query. Non-query sources keep all internal edges in G_mask because their references are labels for no query; masking the heldout of every eligible source would be a protocol deviation requiring an ADR.",
    "Reciprocal pairs with no heldout direction remain in G_mask per GRAPH_PROTOCOL §1.3 ('giữ nguyên tính có hướng trong raw'); every pair with a heldout direction is removed in both directions (audited: two_way_heldout_residual = 0).",
    "Works with missing or out-of-range publication year stay as graph nodes (consistent with the SG-014/SG-015 gate statistics) but can be neither queries nor candidates and never enter a cutoff-induced subgraph.",
    "heldout_count ceil is computed with exact rational arithmetic (Fraction(str(heldout_fraction))) to avoid binary floating-point boundary drift.",
    "Edges whose target year exceeds the source year (both years known) remain in E_pre and G_mask as observed data; time legality is enforced only inside cutoff-induced features (GRAPH_PROTOCOL §3.2).",
    "If post-floor query selection drops below minimum_dev_queries/minimum_test_queries the build fails loudly instead of emitting a below-floor split.",
    "qrels/BEIR labels are never read (track B independent); cited_by_count is never used as a feature (Protocol v1 forbidden features)."
  ],
